```cpp
class MyBuffer {
public:
    int* data;
    size_t size;
    MyBuffer(size_t s) : data(new int[s]), size(s) {} // Manages raw array
    ~MyBuffer() { delete[] data; } // User-defined destructor
    // Now also needs copy constructor, copy assignment,
    // move constructor, and move assignment to be correctly implemented.
};
```
This class directly manages a raw C-style array `data`, requiring a user-defined destructor. This immediately triggers the Rule of Three/Five/Six.
